# Curriculum Overview

## What is Problem Solving with AI about?
 
#### As AI becomes increasingly integrated into daily life, students need to move beyond simply using AI tools—they must develop the skills to critically evaluate, refine, and apply AI-generated content in responsible ways. This unit introduces students to AI as a collaborator in analytical and creative work, helping them explore where AI succeeds, where it fails, and how human oversight improves AI-driven problem solving.

#### This unit blends hands-on AI experimentation with critical evaluation and refinement, guiding students through an iterative cycle of testing, analyzing, and improving AI-generated outputs. Instead of passively accepting AI responses, students will actively investigate AI's reasoning, challenge its assumptions, and refine its outputs through computational thinking and ethical frameworks.


#### **This is the first unit in the six unit <a href='https://code.org/en-US/curriculum/artificial-intelligence-foundations' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>AI Foundations</a> semester 1 course. This professional learning module prepares you to teach it!**


## Student Learning Goals
